## New Capabilities Identified

- **Inline body-link extraction**: build tool scans each page's Markdown body (frontmatter excluded) for standard `[text](url)` links, distinct from the `[[slug|title]]` wikilink syntax already used for `Related`/`Referenced By` edges.
- **`sourceLinks` schema field**: new per-node array (0–5 `{ text, url }` pairs) in `graph-data.json`, capped at the first 5 links found in document order, no deduplication.
- **"Cited sources" side-panel section**: renders below "Connected pages"; omitted entirely (no heading, no empty-list placeholder) when a node has zero extracted links — mirrors the existing empty-description omission precedent (`TOR-04-olJvPNV`).

## Priority Signal

User explicitly requested the 5-link cap upfront ("first 5 max links that are found... limit it and make it contained") to keep the feature scoped and avoid an open-ended extraction/display surface. No other capabilities (e.g., a "+N more" overflow control, deduplication, external-vs-internal URL filtering) were requested — deliberately deferred rather than gold-plated.

## Deferred Items

- Overflow affordance for links beyond the 5-link cap (explicitly out of scope per user direction — "contained" was the stated goal).
- Deduplication of repeated URLs within a page.
- Distinguishing internal (relative/vault) links from external links in extraction or display.
